(14,'KEEP',[II],'numerical','Membrane wave superposition and possible nodal/amplitude images','The source expressly substitutes an ideal membrane with fixed/free boundaries for an elastic plate. Ordinary wave eigenmodes and superposition constrain images; simulation and optional apparatus remain one task.'),
(15,'KEEP',[I],'theory','Low-viscosity capillary-rise dynamics and overshoot','Wetting, tube geometry and negligible-viscosity regime are specified. Surface-tension pressure, gravity and incoming-fluid momentum balance give one-dimensional motion. Variable liquid mass requires care but no unsupplied specialized flow instability.'),
(16,'KEEP',[I,II,VI],'theory','Nonlinear oscillations near a tetrahedral electrostatic equilibrium','Charge symmetry and Coulomb potential expansion determine the constrained restoring force and amplitude-period dependence. The motion line and finite-amplitude approximation require interpretation, not a new physical theory.'),
(17,'KEEP',[VI],'experimental','Four-contact resistance across a two-conductivity sheet interface','The A/B current and C/D voltage diagram was inspected. Local Ohm law, current continuity and interface matching determine potential/resistance using standard electrostatics mathematics.'),
(18,'KEEP',[I,II],'theory','Pulsatile hydraulic flow through a compliant chamber and resistance','The source supplies the chamber/resistance model and sinusoidal-squared input. Linear compliance plus volume balance and the defined hydraulic resistance give a driven first-order equation; biological context adds no necessary physiology.'),
(19,'KEEP',[IV],'numerical','Changing cylinder shape under conductive heating and melting','The microgravity, still-air, no-radiation setup is explicit. Fourier heat flow, sensible heat and latent-heat balance define the moving melting surface. Numerical boundary tracking is mathematics, without an unsupplied crystal or fracture model.'),
(20,'KEEP',[X,XI],'numerical','Temperature dependence of visible incandescent-light efficacy','Planck spectral radiation, photon/energy flux and visible sensitivity weighting estimate the change in apparent illumination and efficacy. Eye spectral response and tungsten emissivity are calibration data, not a new specialized law.'),
(21,'KEEP',[X],'theory','Imaging through a supplied negative-index slab and chromatic error','Negative refractive index is a stated optical model. Snell rays, wavelength-dependent index and image geometry determine focusing and aberration reduction. A microscopic metamaterial realization is not required by the task.'),
(22,'KEEP',[X,XI],'numerical','Lunar corner-cube laser return, diffraction and photon arrival times','Array/element sizes, telescope, energy and pulse duration are explicit and the array photo was checked. Gaussian/aperture diffraction, reflection, path delays and photon energy determine return scale and count. No new laser generation model is needed.'),
(23,'KEEP',[I,VI,VII],'experimental','Electron charge-to-mass measurement by magnetic beam focusing','The complete instrument dimensions and intact acceleration voltage were read from the render. Electrostatic energy, Lorentz helical motion and solenoid current-field relation give speed and first refocus; measurement design is eligible.'),
