(27,'REJECT',[],'theory','Satellite clock equality including special and general relativity','Time-dilation and gravitational-redshift laws are named but not supplied. These control the synchronous altitude and rotation correction; ordinary orbital mechanics alone cannot give them.'),
(28,'BORDERLINE',[VI,VII],'theory','Differential momentum representation and gauge/topological unitary equivalence','Position/momentum operators and the target unitary equation are explicit, supporting substantial differential-operator mathematics. Canonical commutation requirements and physical representation/domain conventions are not defined. Intended self-contained mathematics versus an unsupplied quantum prerequisite remains ambiguous.'),
(29,'REJECT',[],'numerical','Quantum spin rotation, adiabatic limits and measurement probability','The time-dependent spin Hamiltonian is supplied but Schrodinger time evolution and Born measurement rules are not. These determine every probability/polarization trajectory; the task is not merely diagonalizing a finite matrix.'),
(30,'REJECT',[],'theory','Sudden two-spin coupling and failure of perturbative transition probability','Spin-coupling operator and one basis relation are given, but spin operator matrix rules, time-dependent perturbation and quantum transition probabilities are not. They centrally control the exact and approximate comparisons.'),
(31,'REJECT',[],'theory','Spin-two rotation symmetry, Berry phases and state-space topology','One state and coherent-state condition are given. Spin rotations, time-reversal action and Berry geometric phase rules are unsupplied and dominate all symmetry/phase/homotopy tasks.'),
(32,'REJECT',[],'theory','Effect of an unread intervening quantum measurement','Energies and basis vectors alone do not supply unitary time evolution, Born probabilities or unread-measurement state update. Those specialized rules are central to both compared scenarios.'),
(33,'REJECT',[],'numerical','Quantum coherent-state basis and oscillator number-state expansion','Coherent states, their completeness/normalization and number-state construction are not defined. These unsupplied quantum-oscillator rules are the sole physical model requested.'),
(34,'REJECT',[],'theory','Heisenberg motion under a momentum-dependent matrix quantum Hamiltonian','The dyadic Hamiltonian is supplied, but Heisenberg evolution, canonical commutators and wavepacket expectation rules are not. They control position evolution and its physical interpretation.'),
(35,'REJECT',[],'theory','Hydrogen Stark multipole splittings from polygonal external charges','Ordinary Coulomb geometry is only an opening. The central p,d,f shifts require unsupplied hydrogen wavefunctions, degenerate perturbation and Stark selection rules; hyperfine/Lamb comparisons further depend on specialized data.'),
(36,'KEEP',[IX,XI],'theory','Analytical approximation to a quantum model explicitly supplied by a linked paper','The source explicitly links arXiv:1605.01087. Its Sections II-III and Appendix supply a closed scalar expectation-value ODE system, definitions and permitted factorizations. Weak-coupling expansion and integration of those supplied equations answer the requested approximation with ordinary mathematics, without deriving missing quantum rules.'),
(37,'BORDERLINE',[I],'theory','Newtonian hierarchical binary stability with abrupt mass loss and wave disruption','Newtonian point-mass estimates and the mass-loss fraction are expressly allowed, covering substantial tidal stability/orbit work. The final direct gravitational-wave disruption may require a wave-to-tidal-acceleration model not supplied. Whether the intended estimate means only mass-loss effects is unclear.'),
(38,'KEEP',[I,II],'theory','Decreasing-frequency gravitational sources under supplied radiation rates','Strain, frequency relation and orbital radiation-evolution equations are explicitly provided. Combining them with Newtonian energy exchange among point masses permits leading-order configurations and orbital-element evolution. No additional unsupplied GR emission law is necessary.'),
